25	// k-core decomposition by peeling.  Assumes a symmetric graph.
26	//
27	// Degrees[v] holds the degree of v in the graph induced by the vertices that
28	// have not been peeled off yet, and is set to 0 once v is removed.  For
29	// k = 1, 2, ... we repeatedly remove every remaining vertex whose induced
30	// degree is below k; each such vertex belongs to the (k-1)-core but not to the
31	// k-core, so its core number is k-1.  Once a round removes nothing we have
32	// reached a fixed point (the remaining vertices form the k-core) and move on to
33	// k+1.  The largest core number is k-1 for the first k whose core is empty.
